  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653. RNA is clearly dominant over image (0.65 vs 0.21 image-only resnet50), and scvi_n200 + multiprofile is the strongest RNA configuration. The key unresolved question is whether multimodal fusion can add complementary signal beyond the 0.653 RNA-only ceiling. This experiment tests the most promising multimodal extension: scvi_n200 (best RNA encoder), multiprofile (biggest single boost observed), transformer aggregation (marginally best), and imagenet_vit_l (a stronger image encoder than the weak resnet50, which scored only 0.21 standalone) with concat fusion. If this cannot beat 0.653, multimodal is likely not fruitful and remaining budget should focus on RNA-only refinements. If it does, we have a new best to build on. This is the best use of experiment 7 because it directly tests the highest-leverage unexplored direction (can a better image encoder + fusion surpass the RNA-only ceiling?) while keeping all other components at their empirically best settings, isolating the multimodal contribution."
}

